=== PARITY (vs web EnergyFlowWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources → bound via the shared state-holder seam (EnergyFlowSource → EnergyFlowModel):
    useVehicles, useVehicleState(id, refetchInterval 5s), useTranslation. The production app wires
    EnergyFlowSource over the KMP VehiclesStore (StateHolderModel<LoadableState<…>>), resolving the
    selected vehicle the way the web's `vehicleId ?? vehicles[0].id` does; the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection → EnergyFlowBuilder.buildProjection is a 1:1 port of the web memoized nodes/arrows:
    nodes [battery(left,%,emerald,BatteryCharging), motor(right,kW,purple,Zap — label Consuming/
    Regenerating/Standby by sign), charger(top,kW,amber,Plug — only while charging)]; arrows
    battery→motor (consuming, cyan), motor→battery (regen, emerald), charger→battery (amber, charging).
    Stroke ∝ magnitude (1..4); compact keeps the 3 largest. Verified by EXECUTED XCTest (28/28) below.
  Composition → glass widget shell (Activity→`waveform.path.ecg` neon-cyan + "Energy Flow" title +
    freshness chip + refresh + optional Open) · EnergyFlowDiagram (Canvas-stroked arrows with
    marching-dash flow + node circles: SF Symbol in the node color, live value, label outside the ring).
    Recharts→none / Leaflet→none. Web SVG <line>/<circle>/<foreignObject> → Canvas + positioned SwiftUI
    views (crisp symbols + numericText value). lucide→SF: Activity→waveform.path.ecg, BatteryCharging→
    battery.100percent.bolt, Zap→bolt.fill, Plug→powerplug.fill.
  States (all render) → loading (skeleton chrome) · empty ("No energy data available", web `state?…:EmptyState`) ·
    error (Retry) · stale (chip + banner) · offline (cached + chip + banner) · content. Model phase
    resolution keeps cached content visible behind refresh/errors (web shell behavior). The web shell only
    passes `isError` (freshness), so the prompt-required hard-error state (no cache) renders a Retry
    affordance, matching the 0056 precedent.
  i18n → all source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade with the web t(key,default) fallback. Used-vs-
    defined key diff = 0 drift (22 used == 22 defined, incl. the digit-bearing a11y keys). No English
    literals in native code (every Text routes through EnergyFlowStrings / Text(verbatim:)).
  a11y → the diagram is one image element with a localized label ("Energy flow diagram") + a per-node
    value summary (EnergyFlowAccessibility.summary, e.g. "Battery 72%. Consuming 18.4 kW. Charger 11.0 kW");
    every button (refresh / retry / open) has an accessibilityLabel; Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce Motion
    pauses the dash + snaps the value roll.
  Telemetry → EnergyFlowModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"EnergyFlowWidget") → bridges the shared
    Telemetry.track(.screenView) (P1/S11). Asserted by a spy test.
  Registry → EnergyFlowWidget.registration: id "energy-flow", category "battery", default 2×4, min 2×4,
